.TH V4LINUX 1 "October 27, 2026" "unix4-toolchain" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v4linux \- PDP-11 (11/45+EIS) Emulator and UNIX V4 translation layer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v4linux
.RB [ \-r\ \fIroot\fR ] [ \-\-chdir\ \fIdir\fR ] [ \-\-host ] [ \-x ] [ \-s ] [ \-t ] [ \-F ] [ \-f ] [ \-b ] [ \-T ] [ \-o\ \fIfile\fR ]
.I prog args ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I v4linux
is an execution environment for UNIX Fourth Edition PDP-11 programs. It allows the user to run guest binaries as if they are a native Linux binary.
.PP
The following command line options may be used:
.TP
.B \-r \fIroot\fR
Specify the root directory for the guest environment.
.TP
.B \-\-chdir \fIdir\fR
Change the working directory within the guest environment to \fIdir\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-host
Enable host integrations, allowing the guest to interact with the host system.
.TP
.B \-x
Stop execution immediately upon the first \fBexec\fR call.
.TP
.B \-t
Trace every CPU instruction executed by the guest.
.TP
.B \-s
Trace guest system calls (similar to the behavior of \fBstrace\fR).
.TP
.B \-F
Trace floating-point (FPU) instructions.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-trace-func
Trace function calls and their corresponding arguments.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-backtrace
Print a stack backtrace automatically if the guest program crashes.
.TP
.B \-T
Enable all tracing options (\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-s\fR, \fB\-F\fR, \fB\-f\fR) and enable backtracing on crash.
.TP
.B \-o \fIfile\fR
Write the resulting trace output to \fIfile\fR instead of standard output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The behavior of \fBv4linux\fR can also be configured using environment variables.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_CPU=1
Equivalent to \fB\-t\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_SYS=1
Equivalent to \fB\-s\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_FPU=1
Equivalent to \fB\-F\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_FUNC=1
Equivalent to \fB\-f\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_STACK=1
Equivalent to \fB\-b\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_ALL=1
Equivalent to \fB\-T\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_STOP_AT_EXEC=1
Equivalent to \fB\-x\fR.
.TP
.B V4LINUX_TRACE_FILE=path
Equivalent to \fB\-o path\fR.